Language English
Debug Off

Book Chapel Ordered No Keep Looped
	Page Place
		Triggered By @ExploreChapelViaLibrary
		
		Remove TokenExploreChapelViaLibrary
		Add TileChapel, TokenChapelTrapdoor!, TokenChapelWall!
		
		Prolog """
			The door behind the bookcase now stands unlocked.
			You are not sure you truly want to see what lies
			beyond it, but curiosity wins. You glance
			around, then reach for the door...
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Text """
			You grasp the handle and pull. Beyond it
			yawns the mouth of a dark tunnel. You step
			inside, but soon the darkness grows so deep
			that you must feel your way along the smooth
			stone walls.

			Eventually, you notice faint light slipping
			through a crack above. A staircase leads up.
			You climb and push open a door set in the
			ceiling.

			You emerge into an old chapel. Through one
			of its distant windows, you can see the house
			you were hired to clean.

			Place the {c:TileChapel} tile, wall, and trap door as
			indicated, then discard this Explore token. Move 1 space into the
			Chapel.
		"""
		
		$mythosChapel = true
		
		exploredChapel = true
		wandererInLibrary = false
	End Page Place

	Page PlaceExploreOutsideViaChapelLocked
		Add TokenExploreEscapeViaChapelLocked!

		Text """
			Across the room is the chapel's front door.
			Place an Explore token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceExploreOutsideViaChapelLocked

	Page PlaceWhiskey
		Add TokenSearchChapelWhiskey!
		
		Text """
			The room is clean and carefully maintained.

			Strangely, a bottle rests on one of the pews.
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceWhiskey

	Page PlaceSearchRitualComponents
		Add TokenSearchChapelRitualComponents!
		
		Text """
			A ceremonial table stands at the front of
			the room. A large book rests upon it beside
			several religious icons and implements.
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""

		Exit
	End Page PlaceSearchRitualComponents

	Page ExploreEscapeViaChapelLocked
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreEscapeViaChapelLocked
		
		Prolog """
			You pull out a ring of keys and begin trying
			them in the lock.
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Text """
			As you test each key, you hesitate.
			Whatever is happening here could follow
			you, even if you leave now.

			You draw a breath and turn back toward the
			room. Discard this Explore token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenExploreEscapeViaChapelLocked

		Exit
	End Page ExploreEscapeViaChapelLocked

	Page SearchRitualComponents
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchChapelRitualComponents
		
		Prolog """
			You approach the altar. A large book lies
			open upon it.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text QItemRitualComponents """
			As you circle the altar for a closer look,
			you notice a chalice, bundles of herbs, and
			even a skull. As you move to tuck the skull
			into your bag, you reflect on the many times
			you have faced scenes like this.

			Experience has taught you to take anything
			that might prove useful, no matter how
			unlikely. Gain the
			{c:QItemRitualComponents} Unique Item.

			The book is the Smythe family bible. Its
			first pages record births, marriages, and
			deaths stretching back generations. Several
			of the men---all named Smythe---have a
			{success} beside their names.

			{c:EventChosenInvestigator}'s cousin
			Matthias bears that same mark. You do not
			know its meaning, but after what you have
			seen today, it troubles you.

			Gain 2 {clue}, then discard this Search token.
		"""

		Remove TokenSearchChapelRitualComponents
		
		foundRitualComponents = true
		Exit
	End Page SearchRitualComponents

	Page SearchWhiskey
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchChapelWhiskey
		
		Prolog """
			A liquor bottle rests here. The edges of
			its label have been picked at. It is about
			half-full.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text QItemWhiskey """
			You bend to pick it up and casually sniff
			the bottle.

			That is some excellent whiskey. Gain the
			{c:QItemWhiskey} Common Item, then discard
			this Search token.
		"""

		Remove TokenSearchChapelWhiskey
		
		$mythosMinor = true
		Goto SearchWhiskeyNoise
	End Page SearchWhiskey

	Page SearchWhiskeyNoise
		Not Visible
		Add TokenChapelPriestAlive!
		
		Text """
			While you are bent over retrieving the
			bottle, you fail to notice the chapel door
			swing open and a priest step inside.

			Without glancing around, he walks along the
			back wall and turns toward the front.

			As you stand, pleased with your find, your
			shirt catches on a pew. You stumble and
			crash to the floor, letting out a loud curse.

			The priest turns, his expression shifting
			from startled to furious. <<Who are you and
			how did you get in here?>>

			Place the White Man token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page SearchWhiskeyNoise

	Page TalkToPriest
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @TalkToChapelPriest
		
		Text "The priest glares at you expectantly. You respond, ..."
		
		Button 1, "{action} <<What are <i>you</i> doing here?!>>"
		Button 2, "{action} <<I'm with a cleaning service and I got lost.>>"
		Button 3, "{action} In for a penny, in for a pound: kill him."
		Button 4, "Cancel"
		
		If selection = 4 Then Mark Unread
		If selection = 4 Then Exit
		
		If selection = 1 Then Goto KillPriest
		if selection = 2 Then Goto TruthToPriest
		Goto KillPriest
	End Page TalkToPriest

	Page TruthToPriest
		Not Visible
		
		Text QItemRitualDagger """
			<<Oh,>> the priest says, brightening.
			<<Benjamin told me you would be here today.
			I am not sure how you found this place, but
			you should return to the house and get to
			work. The family needs it cleaned properly.

			<<I will remind the boys you are here at
			Benjamin's request.>>

			The priest turns and walks outside, leaving
			you unsettled.

			Discard the White Man token.

			As you consider everything, you glance down
			and notice he dropped something. Wrapped in
			cloth is an ornate knife. Gain the
			{c:QItemRitualDagger} Common Item.

			<<A haunted house, murdered children, and
			now what looks like a local cult,>> you
			mutter. <<What have I gotten myself into?>>
		"""
		
		Remove TokenChapelPriest
		
		wandererFrequency = wandererFrequency + 2
		Goto PlaceSearchCryptViaChapel
	End Page TruthToPriest

	Page PlaceSearchCryptViaChapel
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenSearchCryptViaChapel!
		
		Text """
			While you are bent down, you notice something odd about the floor.
			
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page

	Page KillPriest
		Not Visible
		
		Text QItemRitualDagger """
			You draw back your arm and strike. The
			priest raises his hands too late.

			Your fist connects with his temple. He
			staggers, falls backward, and strikes his
			head against the corner of a pew.

			He seizes briefly, then lies still. He is
			dead.

			You look down at the body and notice
			something slipping from his robes. Gain the
			{c:QItemRitualDagger}.

			<<A haunted house, dead children, and now
			a local cult,>> you mutter. <<I should leave
			before someone finds this latest body.>>

			Discard the White Man token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenChapelPriestAlive

		chapelPriestDead = 1
		wandererMax = wandererMax + 1
		If wandererMax > 6 Then WandererMax = 6
		wandererFrequency = wandererFrequency - 1
		
		Goto PlaceSearchCryptViaChapel
	End Page KillPriest

	Page DefeatRiot
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @DefeatedCustomMonsterChapelRiot

		Text QItemRitualDagger """
			The priest and his men lie dead at your
			feet, their blood seeping into the wooden
			floor.

			<<A haunted house, dead children, and now
			a local cult,>> you mutter. <<I should get
			out of here before anyone else arrives.>>

			You glance over the carnage and think,
			<i>Perhaps there is something useful
			here?</i> Then you see it---something
			slipping from the priest's robe.

			Gain the {c:QItemRitualDagger}.
		"""
		
		chapelPriestDead = 1
		
		// add a wanderer and shorten the time between them
		wandererMax = wandererMax + 1
		If wandererMax > 6 Then WandererMax = 6
		wandererFrequency = wandererFrequency - 1
		
		Goto PlaceSearchCryptViaChapel
	End Page

	Page SearchRitualDagger
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchChapelRitualDagger If Unread
		
		Prolog """
			The priest lies motionless at your feet.
			Before searching his robes, perhaps you
			should be certain he is truly dead.
		"""
		Button "Make sure he's dead"
		
		Text QItemRitualDagger """
			You step closer and nudge the body lightly
			with your foot.

			Nothing.

			Growing bolder, you kick him harder. The
			body rolls limply onto its side. As it
			turns, his robes fall open, revealing an
			ornate knife wrapped in cloth.

			Gain the {c:QItemRitualDagger} Common Item.

			<<Did any of you see his right hand
			twitch?>>
		"""
		
		foundRitualDagger = true
		Trigger @AnotherRequirementCompleted
		Exit
	End Page SearchRitualDagger

	Page SearchRitualDaggerAfter
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchChapelRitualDagger If SearchRitualDagger Is Read	
		
		Prolog "The priest's fingers twitch slightly."
		Button "Make sure he's dead"
		
		Text """
			The priest is dead and you're seeing things.

			You should leave the priest alone
			and focus on the task at hand.

			Discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenChapelPriest
		Exit
	End Page SearchRitualDaggerAfter

	Page SearchCryptViaChapel
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchCryptViaChapel
		
		Prolog """
			Something about this place feels wrong.
			You crouch to examine the wooden floor
			more closely.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text """
			One floorboard sits slightly uneven among
			the others. It appears more worn as well.
			You press it. It shifts, but only a little.

			You stand up and step onto it with more weight. The
			panel sinks and clicks. The wall before
			you swings open. Discard the wall and
			this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchCryptViaChapel
		Remove TokenChapelWall
		
		Goto SearchCryptViaChapel2
	End Page SearchCryptViaChapel

	Page SearchCryptViaChapel2
		Not Visible
		
		Add TileCrypt
		
		Text """
			You pull the wall aside, revealing a
			doorway sealed by a heavy stone door.
			You push against it.

			Place the {c:TileCrypt} tile.
		"""
		
		If exploredCrypt Then Text """
			You pull the wall aside and reveal a
			stone-sealed doorway. You push against
			it and it opens easily.

			<<This
			is another door to the crypt we found
			earlier,>> you say.
		"""
		
		If Not exploredCrypt Then Trigger @ExploreCryptViaChapel

		Exit
	End Page SearchCryptViaChapel2

End Book Chapel